	I ran into the same problem with my Amiga 1000, HD, 1.5MB ram.

	You need to edit the configuration file and remove the RAMDISK
	assignment.  If a RAMDISK is present, the game seems to use it
	to store levels, and there is just not enough memory on a 1MB
	system (or even a 1.5MB system!) to have both the game and a
	RAMDISK hanging around in memory!

	Good luck!


